# DHAIRYA & SMIT GOGRI LTD — Corporate Website

A lightweight, multi-page static corporate site designed to support a UK public-sector tender submission while keeping unsupported claims clearly separated from verified company/portfolio facts.

## Technology choice

The site uses plain HTML5, CSS3 and vanilla JavaScript. There is no build system and no runtime dependency. This is deliberate: the site can be hosted cheaply and securely on GitHub Pages, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages or any standard static host, loads quickly, and is easy to audit.

## Structure

- `index.html` — home / corporate positioning
- `about.html` — company information and background
- `services.html` — service capabilities and delivery method
- `team.html` — proposed nine-role delivery model (illustrative names; replace before submission)
- `projects.html` — portfolio-backed technical work + illustrative map concept
- `tender-alignment.html` — explicit mapping of published notice requirements to site evidence
- `policies.html` — operating controls and procurement-friendly commitments
- `evidence-register.html` — bid-evidence matrix separating proven facts, proposals and missing supporting documents
- `privacy.html` — plain-English website privacy information
- `404.html` — static-hosting fallback page
- `contact.html` — corporate contact details + form demonstration
- `css/styles.css` — global responsive styles
- `js/site.js` — navigation and small page helpers
- `js/map-demo.js` — map concept filter interaction
- `assets/mark.svg` — lightweight brand mark
- `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` — deployment options and configuration
- `docs/TESTING.md` — testing and re-test instructions

## Important bid-use notes

1. The public tender notice (083205-2026) contains a high-level scope. It does not publish a detailed supplier qualification schedule or full technical specification. The site deliberately does not invent certifications, insurance limits, financial tests or named staff evidence.
2. The nine team profiles are illustrative placeholders. Replace them with authorised, real personnel and factual CV information before using the website as evidence in a bid.
3. The projects page contains technical/academic portfolio work from the founder's existing website and public GitHub repositories. It does not present those projects as previous commercial contracts for DHAIRYA & SMIT GOGRI LTD.
4. The map concept is explicitly illustrative; it is not presented as a council-approved or already-delivered Witney solution.

## Accuracy and bid integrity

This site is written to strengthen credibility without manufacturing credentials. Replace every illustrative personnel entry before bid use, attach documentary evidence for any insurance/financial/certification requirement, and align the formal tender response to the buyer's complete tender documents in the procurement portal.
